─── Description ───
  Same pattern as @01KHZ941 but for other generated files. kspec setup and skill rendering should skip writing files when content hasn't changed, avoiding unnecessary git diffs. Audit all generation paths (skills, setup output) and apply the same hash-check-before-write pattern.
Created:   2026-02-21T05:13:53.619Z
Started:   2026-02-23T09:55:12.581Z

─── Notes ───
[2026-02-23T08:51:46.498Z] @claude:
AUTOMATION: Standalone optimization. Apply hash-check-before-write pattern to skill rendering paths. No spec needed.
[2026-02-23T10:07:14.501Z] @claude:
Implemented hash-check-before-write for: (1) generateAgentInstructions in setup.ts — uses metaHash comparison to skip kspec-agents.md regeneration when unchanged, displays 'already up to date' in setup output. (2) copyCoreSkillFiles in skill-install.ts — compares SKILL.md content and supporting directory trees before copying, returns { changed: boolean } so callers can track changes. (3) Guard script writes in installClaudeCodeHooks — reads existing script content before writing, skips write if identical. All 3181 tests pass.

